---
import DocsLayout from '~/layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
---

<DocsLayout title="Documentation" description="Kotoshu documentation index — Ruby API, CLI reference, configuration, caching, plugins, migration, and tool comparison.">
  <p class="docs-lead">Guides and reference for the Kotoshu engine on every channel — the Ruby gem and CLI, the Python, JavaScript, Rust, and Go clients, the HTTP server, the editor LSP, and the GitHub Action.</p>

  <p class="eyebrow mb-3"><span class="jp" lang="ja">接続</span>Clients & channels</p>
  <h2 class="display text-2xl mt-12">Eight ways in, one engine</h2>
  <p class="text-[15px] leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)] mt-4">
    Whatever you install talks to the same checking core. Each channel page carries an install
    command, a quick start that was actually executed, and the capability notes — what is native,
    what goes over the wire. Start from the
    <a href="/install" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">channel catalog</a> if you
    are not sure which is yours.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div>
      <a href="/docs/clients/python" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Python client</a>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">pip install kotoshu — the HTTP client, plus the kotoshu-native wheel for offline checking in-process.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a href="/docs/clients/javascript" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">JavaScript client</a>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">npm install @kotoshu/client — typed HTTP client and the @kotoshu/wasm engine for Node, Deno, Bun, and browsers.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a href="/docs/clients/rust" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Rust engine</a>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">cargo add kotoshu — the engine itself: dictionaries, ranked suggest, the KOSH batch ABI, the models registry.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a href="/docs/clients/go" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Go client</a>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">go get kotoshu-go — context-aware check, suggest, detect, correct over the HTTP API.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a href="/docs/clients/http" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">HTTP API server</a>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">Seven JSON endpoints over Rack and Puma — the contract every SDK speaks, with an OpenAPI 3.1 spec.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a href="/docs/clients/lsp" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Editor (LSP)</a>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">gem install kotoshu-lsp — diagnostics, quick-fixes, and hover suggestions in Neovim, VS Code, Emacs.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a href="/docs/clients/action" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">GitHub Action</a>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">kotoshu/action-kotoshu@v1 — SARIF in the Security tab, dictionaries cached between runs.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="eyebrow mb-3 mt-16"><span class="jp" lang="ja">参照</span>Reference</p>
  <h2 class="display text-2xl mt-12">The gem, documented</h2>
  <p class="text-[15px] leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)] mt-4">
    The Ruby gem has a deliberately small surface: one facade module, one CLI, three
    caches. These pages document each piece as it exists today — where something
    is a roadmap item rather than a feature, the text says so.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div>
      <a href="/docs/api" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Ruby API</a>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">The facade module: two-stage resources, checking, suggestions, detection, and the optional semantic path.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a href="/docs/cli" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">CLI reference</a>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]"><code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">check</code>, <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">setup</code>, <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">cache</code>, <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">completions</code> — flags, defaults, stdin, and exit codes.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a href="/docs/configuration" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Configuration</a>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">Resolution order, KOTOSHU_* environment variables, XDG paths, dictionary types, and the personal dictionary.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a href="/docs/caching" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Caching</a>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">The three resource caches, SHA-256 integrity, TTLs, offline mode, and management commands.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a href="/docs/plugins" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Plugins</a>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">Custom dictionary types, custom suggestion strategies, and document-format plugin gems.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a href="/docs/migration" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Migrating</a>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">From hunspell, aspell, cspell, or LanguageTool — what transfers and what does not.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <a href="/docs/comparison" class="font-medium text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Comparison</a>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">An honest feature table next to hunspell, cspell, and LanguageTool.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-8 rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-bg-inset)] p-5 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-text-2)]">
    <p>
      New here? The <a href="/install" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">install page</a>
      is the sixty-second path from
      <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-[var(--color-accent)]">gem install kotoshu</code>
      to a checked document. For what changed and when, see the
      <a href="/news" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">news section</a>;
      for the complete generated method reference,
      <a href="https://rubydoc.info/gems/kotoshu" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">rubydoc.info/gems/kotoshu</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
